Portions of this software are derived from imgproxy
================================================================================

The following directories contain source code copied from, or derived from,
the imgproxy project:

    internal/processing/
    internal/options/
    internal/security/
    internal/vips/          (Go and C sources)
    internal/imagetype/
    internal/imagemeta/
    internal/auximageprovider/
    internal/env/
    internal/bufreader/
    internal/errctx/
    internal/ioutil/
    internal/imath/
    internal/ensure/

    imgproxy
    https://github.com/imgproxy/imgproxy
    Copyright (c) imgproxy contributors
    Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0

A copy of the Apache License, Version 2.0 is provided in LICENSE-imgproxy.

Modifications made by iStore are described in README.md under
"What was changed relative to imgproxy". In summary:

  * internal/vips no longer depends on imgproxy's `imagedata` and `options`
    packages; it uses iStore's own internal/imagedata and takes save options
    from process configuration.
  * internal/env dropped aws.go, gcp.go and load.go, which resolve values via
    AWS Secrets Manager, AWS SSM and GCP Secret Manager.
  * imgproxy's `server` package was replaced by internal/timeout, which carries
    the single function (CheckTimeout) that the pipeline used.
  * imgproxy's `options/parser` package was removed; iStore parses the
    x-oss-process grammar instead.
  * SVG support was removed: internal/imagetype/svg.go (detection) and
    imgproxy's processing/svg (sanitizing), both of which need `xmlparser`.
  * auximageprovider loads auxiliary images from disk only, not over HTTP.
  * Environment variable prefix changed from IMGPROXY_ to ISTORE_.
  * Tests and test helpers were not carried over.
  * internal/vips gained two operations that imgproxy does not have:
    vips_linear_go (a linear transform of the colour bands) and
    vips_round_corners_go (a rounded-rectangle alpha mask), together with the
    Image.Linear and Image.RoundCorners methods that call them.
  * internal/processing gained two pipeline steps that imgproxy does not have,
    adjust.go (brightness and contrast) and round_corners.go (circle and
    rounded corners), and the corresponding options keys and accessors.

